+// Anarva: seconds until a job does its job, the one scale every builder job shares. An economy job (it extracts or
+// makes energy) returns its cost only after paying it back: travel + build + payback, payback = cost (energy priced at
+// the converter rate) / the metal-equivalent it adds per second. Other jobs: travel + build + cost / our income. Ranking by time per
+// metal of COST made the most expensive job win: a lab before the extractors that feed it (smoke 2026-11-25).
+// Anarva: production is the least of build power, metal and energy (owner, 2026-11-25). Extra build power spends only
+// the metal we earn and don't spend AND have the energy for, at the energy per metal our factories draw: while energy
+// stalls it is worth nothing (builders assisted the lab with metal full and energy empty, Gasbag minute 4-5).
+// The time a builder commits to one job: an extractor's build time at our average builder's build power (seconds).
+static float AnarvaJobWindow(circuit::CCircuitAI* circuit)
+{
+	circuit::CEconomyManager* eco = circuit->GetEconomyManager();
+	circuit::CBuilderManager* bm = circuit->GetBuilderManager();
+	const float avgBp = bm->GetBuildPower() / std::max(1.f, float(bm->GetWorkerCount()));
+	const circuit::CCircuitDef* mex = eco->GetSideInfo().mexDef;
+	return std::max(1.f, (mex != nullptr) ? mex->GetBuildTime() / std::max(1.f, avgBp) : 1.f);
